This directory is NOT covered by the MIT license in the repository root.

The line-differ here is a port of the xdiff library as it appears in git
(xdiff/xprepare.c, xdiff/xdiffi.c, xdiff/xemit.c), including its record
cleanup heuristic and the indent-heuristic weights. xdiff derives from
LibXDiff:

    LibXDiff by Davide Libenzi ( File Differential Library )
    Copyright (C) 2003  Davide Libenzi <davidel@xmailserver.org>

and carries, in git as in LibXDiff:

    This library is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify it
    under the terms of the GNU Lesser General Public License as published by
    the Free Software Foundation; either version 2.1 of the License, or (at
    your option) any later version.

    This library is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but
    WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
    MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the GNU Lesser
    General Public License for more details.

    You should have received a copy of the GNU Lesser General Public License
    along with this library; if not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.

The port, and any modification of it made here, is distributed under the same
terms. The full licence text is at ../../../LICENSES/LGPL-2.1.txt.

The rest of kompjutr uses this directory as a library and remains MIT. LGPL
2.1 permits that: section 6 covers a work that uses the Library, and nothing
outside this directory is a derivative of it.
